ty":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the safeguard (backup, dry-run, reversible migration, rollback) or justify the irreversibility explicitly (T4).","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture (in an ADR / AGENTS.md / CI doc) why the enforcement lane requires a container/environment with unprivileged user namespaces enabled, so the precondition survives image/runner changes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6612,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Notes: 'GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest runners ... DENY unprivileged user namespaces', so a special environment is required","No doc/ADR deliverable is listed for the new lane's environment requirement"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new gating CI lane whose load-bearing, non-obvious requirement is a container/environment with unprivileged user namespaces ENABLED (so probe() returns non-None), yet no ADR/AGENTS.md/design-doc note captures why this lane needs that specific environment.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd804507e511e021c","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Definition of Done / Notes","norm_id":"n536911cded4b3fa3","priority":0.2888,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer sees the enforcement lane fail after a runner/image change and cannot tell that unprivileged-userns support is the required precondition."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consolidate AC1 and AC3, or state the distinct mechanism AC3 adds beyond AC1's 'outcome is passed, not skipped' assertion (e.g. a lane-level policy that fails the whole lane on any skipped enforcement test).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.73,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'asserting the test's outcome is passed, not skipped, in that lane's report'","AC3: 'A skipped enforcement test is treated as a FAILURE on the lane ... so the silent-skip mode cannot return'"],"finding":"AC1 ('outcome is passed, not skipped') and AC3 ('a skipped enforcement test is treated as a FAILURE') encode the same skip-catching guarantee, creating a near-duplicate criterion without a distinct proving mechanism for AC3.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda71e2dd076bdb34","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, lines 1 and 3","norm_id":"nb017df5a3c158329","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements AC1's outcome assertion and is unsure whether AC3 requires an additional, separate mechanism."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for the container/locally-runnable approach: bwrap enforcement needs unprivileged user namespaces (which ubuntu-latest denies) and those are available inside a privileged/appropriately-configured container, as the e668 ubuntu:24.04 manual run demonstrated.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3487,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC#4: 'The mechanism is portable: it does not depend on a feature unique to one CI provider ... A container image or an equivalent locally-runnable environment satisfies this'","scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:66-84 — probe() returns None unless _bwrap_works() succeeds, which needs unprivileged CLONE_NEWUSER","Plan Notes: bwrap 'WAS verified by hand ... in a ubuntu:24.04 container'","G6 checklist item 4: absence of a positive rationale for the chosen approach is a finding"],"finding":"The plan names an approach FAMILY (AC#4: 'A container image or an equivalent locally-runnable environment') but states no POSITIVE rationale for why that direction fits the problem — specifically the load-bearing fact that bwrap requires unprivileged user namespaces, which GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest denies but a privileged/appropriately-configured container permits (the e668 manual verification ran in ubuntu:24.04).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc548fbd68b95b747","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC#4) / Definition of Done","norm_id":"n082146d5d16192ae","priority":0.2513,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer picks a lane environment that installs bwrap but does not enable user namespaces, silently reproducing the skip"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a short rationale to the plan: the gating lane must run in an environment that PERMITS unprivileged user namespaces (e.g. a privileged container image, matching the ubuntu:24.04 environment the e668 manual verification used) so that mutation_sandbox.probe() returns BWRAP rather than None; that is why a container/locally-runnable env — not a stock ubuntu-latest runner — is the chosen approach.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make explicit that the gating lane's environment must permit unprivileged user namespaces so mutation_sandbox.probe() returns BWRAP (not None); a lane that only trips AC#3's skip-as-failure has still proven nothing about enforcement.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py:62-65 — `live = pytest.mark.skipif(sb.probe() is None, ...)`","scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:82 — `if shutil.which('bwrap') and _bwrap_works()` gates on functional capability, not presence","AC#1: 'executes (does NOT skip) ... asserting the test's outcome is passed, not skipped'"],"finding":"AC#1 (test executes and is 'passed') combined with AC#3 (skip = failure) does not guarantee the lane PROVES enforcement: if the chosen environment does not actually permit unprivileged user namespaces, probe() returns None, the tests skip, and the lane goes red BY SKIP rather than by an enforcement failure — leaving Linux write-denial unproven even on a red lane. The plan does not state that the environment must make probe() return BWRAP.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb69d948a7c805dd","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC#1, AC#3)","norm_id":"n35ccceaced7ecd7b","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Container/runner has bwrap installed but userns disabled: probe() -> None -> @live tests skip -> lane red by AC#3 but enforcement never observed"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequ